From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:22:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Check the passenger before the AI flag in
 getControllingPassenger

Mobs almost never carry a mob passenger, yet every call read the NoAI
synced flag first. Both checks are side-effect free, so testing the
passenger first gives the same result.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java
index 1add5ca9829a07f09fde4bc4eb0964e9103612b1..864af151e87de80536aa91d64a98b2e5c27761b0 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@ public abstract class Mob extends LivingEntity implements Targeting, EquipmentUs
     @Override
     public @Nullable LivingEntity getControllingPassenger() {
         Entity firstPassenger = this.getFirstPassenger();
-        return !this.isNoAi() && firstPassenger instanceof Mob passenger && firstPassenger.canControlVehicle() ? passenger : null;
+        return firstPassenger instanceof Mob passenger && !this.isNoAi() && firstPassenger.canControlVehicle() ? passenger : null; // Pyzh - Check the passenger before reading synced AI flags
     }
 
     public Sensing getSensing() {
